<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia stocks seen holding gains on firm bonds.</title>
<headline>Australia stocks seen holding gains on firm bonds.</headline>
<text>
<p>------------------(Snapshot 8.50 a.m./2250 GMT)----------------</p>
<p>AORD cl	     2584.8 +20.9     DJIA (Fri close)    7345.91</p>
<p>SPI Sycom	   2584.0 +2.0	US 30yr (Fri close)    6.99</p>
<p>10yrbond futs    92.425  +0.045    Gold NY 342.50 Lon fix 342.55</p>
<p>AUD open $0.7680(local cl $0.7676) CRB Index (Fri close) 251.31 NIKKEI	  20,043.50  +34.50    FTSE (Fri close)     4661.8</p>
<p>S&amp;P500   (Fri close)     848.95    NZSE40 open   2311.08  +0.03</p>
<p>--------------------------(May 27)-----------------------------</p>
<p>*Stocks to gains despite some profit-taking, eyes on firm bonds in absence of Dow. &quot;It'll be up, but not aggressively up,&quot; said Burdett, Buckeridge &amp; Young's Graham Buckeridge.  </p>
<p>*Pre-open bids A$18.90 (-0.02), A$18.91 (-0.03), A$5.78 (+0.01), A$8.52 (+0.04)</p>
<p>*Dow closed for holiday, as was U.K. market.</p>
<p>*ADRs: News Corp 17 7/8 (unch), BHP 29 3/4 (unch), WMC 25 5/8 (unch), National Australia Bank 72 3/8 (unch)</p>
<p>*London and New York metal and gold markets closed.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
